name: start
boss: firstlight
flavor: Before you touch anything, you learn how to touch it safely.
brief: This stick carries dozens of tools. Some read a file, some fix a broken
brief: disk, some knock on a computer to find open doors. They are sharp:
brief: pointed at a stranger's machine that is a crime; pointed at your own it
brief: is how you learn and how you defend.
brief:
brief: The whole rest of this school aims every tool at THIS computer, on the
brief: address ``127.0.0.1`` -- which only ever means "me". Never change it to
brief: someone else's.
brief:
brief: The tools live on the encrypted side, which cannot run a program
brief: directly -- that is what keeps the stick safe. `xexec` is the doorway:
brief: it copies one tool into a tiny space that can run, runs it, and tears
brief: that space down. In here the school runs the tools for you; outside,
brief: you run one yourself with ``sh ~/tools/xexec`` then the tool's name.
brief:
brief: You already met `abduco` in the base course -- it keeps a shell alive
brief: even after you disconnect. `dvtm` builds on that: it splits one screen
brief: into panes, so you can watch several things at once. Both are drilled
brief: here.
---
q: {the one safe address to aim every tool at, in this school|what address means "only this machine"|the loopback address the school uses for every target}
a: 127.0.0.1
ref: xexec
teach: xexec
hint: four numbers -- it always means "me", never someone else
---
q: {outside the school, run a carried tool by hand|off the school's rails, get a stick tool running yourself|no school doing it for you now, launch a tool straight from the stick} -- the `xexec` doorway, running ``httpx``
a: sh ~/tools/xexec httpx
a: xexec httpx
ref: xexec
teach: xexec
hint: sh ~/tools/xexec then the tool name
---
q: {see every session you've got running|check which sessions haven't been closed|pull up whatever sessions are still alive}, with `abduco`
a: abduco
ref: abduco
teach: abduco
hint: abduco with no arguments prints the session list
---
q: {kick off a fresh session with a shell inside it|get a new session up and running a shell|open a session that drops you straight into a shell} -- `abduco`, name it ``work``
a: abduco -n work /bin/sh
a: abduco -c work /bin/sh
ref: abduco
teach: abduco
hint: -n (or -c) names a new session, then the program to run
---
q: `dvtm` -- {the keys that open a new pane|what you press to split off a new pane|the shortcut for adding another pane}
a: ctrl-g c
ref: dvtm
teach: dvtm
hint: the dvtm mod key is ctrl-g, then c for a new pane
---
q: `abduco` -- {step back from a session without ending it|pull out of a session while leaving it alive|walk away from a session, keeping it running}
a: ctrl-\
ref: abduco
teach: abduco
hint: ctrl and backslash steps away; abduco -a work returns
